error[KL1010]: label value `team@example.com` of `owner` is invalid: must be empty, or contain only letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.`, and start and end with a letter or digit
 --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:7:12
  |
7 |     owner: team@example.com
  |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = help: use letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.`, for example `team-example.com`; free text belongs in an annotation

error[KL1010]: label key `Team Name` is invalid: its name part must contain only letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.`, and start and end with a letter or digit
 --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:8:5
  |
8 |     Team Name: payments
  |     ^^^^^^^^^
  = help: write the key as an optional lowercase DNS prefix and `/`, then up to 63 letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.`, for example `Team-Name`

error[KL1010]: label `version` has a value that YAML reads as a number, not a string
  --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:17:14
   |
17 |     version: 1.0
   |              ^^^
  = help: quote the value: `version: "1.0"`

error[KL1010]: label `canary` has a value that YAML reads as a boolean, not a string
  --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:18:13
   |
18 |     canary: yes
   |             ^^^
  = help: quote the value: `canary: "yes"`

error[KL1010]: label key `Example.com/tier` is invalid: its prefix must contain only lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `.`, and each part between dots must start and end with a letter or digit
  --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:27:5
   |
27 |     Example.com/tier: web
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = help: write the key as an optional lowercase DNS prefix and `/`, then up to 63 letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.`, for example `example.com/tier`

error[KL1010]: label key `a/b/c` is invalid: may contain at most one `/`, between an optional DNS prefix and the name
  --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:28:5
   |
28 |     a/b/c: x
   |     ^^^^^
  = help: write the key as an optional lowercase DNS prefix and `/`, then up to 63 letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.`, for example `app.kubernetes.io/name`

error[KL1010]: label key `example.com/` is invalid: its name part must be non-empty
  --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:29:5
   |
29 |     example.com/: x
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = help: write the key as an optional lowercase DNS prefix and `/`, then up to 63 letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.`, for example `app.kubernetes.io/name`

